# a vault is user data — never commit
grimoire-vault/
*.tmp
.grimoire/
.playwright-mcp/
/tmp/
docs/GAP-ANALYSIS.md
tools/node_modules/

# built binaries
go/grimoire
go/grimoire-mcp
.verify-artifacts/
dist/

# Artifacts the CLI writes into whatever directory you run it from. `grimoire
# export` defaults to ./grimoire-export/ and `grimoire backup` to
# ./grimoire-backup-<stamp>.tar.gz — and those are an export and a backup of a
# REAL vault: the notes, and .grimoire/secrets.json. Both were committed by
# accident once and had to be purged from history; ignoring them by pattern is
# what stops the next `git add -A` from doing it again.
grimoire-export/
grimoire-backup-*.tar.gz
